            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/processor_metrics.hpp",
                    "line": 156,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JY-Voon",
                        "email": "jvoon@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "JY-Voon"
                    },
                    "message": "I have recently received a comment suggesting not to bind the case of `EBADR` and `boost::system::errc::io_error` together.\n\nNot sure if we should separate them case by case, please check the following link:\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/bmcweb/+/88594/comment/ea19e176_1053d231/"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/processor_metrics.hpp",
                    "line": 168,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JY-Voon",
                        "email": "jvoon@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "JY-Voon"
                    },
                    "message": "Are we expecting `serviceMap.size() == 1` here from the retrieved `associatedSubTree`?\nIf so, I think we can add a log here for better debugging."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/processor_metrics.hpp",
                    "line": 184,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JY-Voon",
                        "email": "jvoon@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "JY-Voon"
                    },
                    "message": "nit: I would prefer the following implementation for better understanding, but it's up to you if you prefer current implementation.\n```\n\ninline std::optional<nlohmann::json::json_pointer> getThrottleDurationJsonPtr(const std::string& metricName)\n{\n    if (metricName == \"power_limit_throttle_duration\")\n    {\n        return \"/PowerLimitThrottleDuration\"_json_pointer;\n    }\n    if (metricName == \"thermal_limit_throttle_duration\")\n    {\n        return \"/ThermalLimitThrottleDuration\"_json_pointer;\n    }\n    return std::nullopt;\n}\n\ninline void afterGetProcessorMetricsThrottleDurations(\n    const std::shared_ptr<bmcweb::AsyncResp>& asyncResp,\n    const boost::system::error_code& ec,\n    const dbus::utility::MapperGetSubTreeResponse& subtree)\n{\n    ...\n    \n    const std::optional<nlohmann::json::json_pointer> jsonPtr{getThrottleDurationJsonPtr(metricName)};\n    \n    if (!jsonPtr) \n    {\n        continue;\n    }\n    getProcessorMetricsThrottleDuration(asyncResp, serviceName, path, jsonPtr);\n}\n\n```"
                }
            ],
